    "title": "Facts, not emotion, should be focus",
    "text": "To the editor:\nThere was an election, and Americans chose Donald Trump over Joe Biden for a number of reasons.\nCertainly they were not looking for a king. They wanted someone who would take action and enforce the laws of the land — particularly at our borders.\nWhile it may be fashionable to shout slogans that perpetuate the many lies we have been told by our press and some in “leadership” positions, our time might be better spent calmly discussing the issues.\nGood discussion requires some discipline over emotion — and some examination of the facts. I wish more who hold up signs, slow traffic and chant would build credible arguments supported by facts.\nMaybe start by comparing what Joe Biden accomplished in his last 100 days with what Trump has accomplished in his first 100.\nBrian Gardner\nPort Avenue",
